03:00.580 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.610 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.650 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.680 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.710 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.740 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.770 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.800 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.830 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:00.860 --> 03:04.990
<b>Episode 10: "Ouka and Kikka"</b>

03:02.250 --> 03:04.380
I didn't know Ouka-chan was a twin.

03:04.380 --> 03:04.990
And?

03:04.990 --> 03:09.500
She said she needed to talk to her, 
so she'd wait until the café closed.

03:09.790 --> 03:11.770
I wonder what she does.

03:11.770 --> 03:14.250
She said she's a college student.

03:14.250 --> 03:15.870
Huh...

03:15.870 --> 03:17.380
Where's Ami-chan, anyway?

03:17.710 --> 03:19.680
The shock left her bedridden.

03:19.680 --> 03:21.760
Doppel... Doppel...

03:21.760 --> 03:25.010
She said she saw online that 
if you see a doppelgänger twice,

03:25.010 --> 03:27.100
you're fated to die.

03:27.100 --> 03:28.770
Uh-huh...

03:29.160 --> 03:31.850
So what's this all about?

03:32.120 --> 03:34.360
Why did you need all of us here?

03:34.780 --> 03:38.320
Our parents asked me to come 
and check on my sister.

03:38.320 --> 03:40.610
She didn't come home for Obon.

03:40.890 --> 03:44.590
Oh, she's her sister? 
I thought she was a doppelgänger!

03:44.590 --> 03:45.620
Please stop.

03:45.620 --> 03:47.850
I called, though.

03:47.850 --> 03:50.620
I said I couldn't come home 
because I was busy at my part-time job.

03:51.370 --> 03:52.650
What does that mean?

03:52.650 --> 03:56.380
You didn't even go to college, 
saying you wanted to be a designer,

03:56.380 --> 03:58.280
and you end up in a part-time job?

03:58.280 --> 03:59.660
W-Well...

03:59.660 --> 04:02.750
And what is this part-time job, anyway?

04:02.750 --> 04:06.190
You said you were a live-in, so I thought 
you'd be in company housing...

04:06.190 --> 04:11.080
but you're living in a house 
with a boy and four other girls?

04:11.520 --> 04:14.020
What is even going on here?

04:14.350 --> 04:18.350
Well... Yeah, I guess it does seem 
pretty weird, doesn't it?

04:18.350 --> 04:22.680
I'm amazed there are no stupid rumors 
about us around town.

04:22.680 --> 04:24.530
It's just a share house!

04:24.840 --> 04:28.160
It's nothing like what 
you're imagining at all.

04:28.160 --> 04:31.660
Maybe not now, but in the future, who knows?

04:32.260 --> 04:35.030
Th-That's never gonna happen!

04:36.220 --> 04:37.900
And what is this?

04:37.900 --> 04:42.840
You've got one girl who looks like 
some hussy that'll seduce any guy...

04:42.840 --> 04:45.800
A scary-looking girl who looks like

04:45.800 --> 04:49.610
she's involved in some fishy business 
with underground connections...

04:50.440 --> 04:56.440
An obviously dumb-looking girl who'd 
instantly do anything a guy asked her to...

04:53.800 --> 04:56.440
Kikka... ika...

04:56.890 --> 05:01.610
And a girl who tries to look too pure 
and sweet to know anything,

05:01.610 --> 05:06.030
but who's probably the most lecherous 
of them all deep down!

05:06.030 --> 05:09.950
H-How mean! That's not what I'm like at all!

05:10.300 --> 05:11.210
Right?!

05:11.210 --> 05:13.030
Shiragiku-san is—

05:13.560 --> 05:17.370
That's right. 
Kiku-chan isn't that kind of girl.

05:17.680 --> 05:19.170
And above all...

05:19.170 --> 05:21.630
This guy calling himself the owner.

05:21.630 --> 05:23.040
He puts on a cool façade,

05:23.040 --> 05:26.930
but this is the type of guy who uses 
his authority to toy with girls!

05:27.320 --> 05:30.270
I bet at least one of you 
has already fallen for him.

05:30.270 --> 05:32.420
You just don't know it yet, Nee-san.

05:33.150 --> 05:36.230
Stop talking like that! You're being rude!

05:36.540 --> 05:40.110
You and I are twins! If that's how I feel,

05:40.110 --> 05:42.610
then it must be how you feel, too, right?!

05:42.610 --> 05:45.860
What?! I never thought any such—

05:46.220 --> 05:49.690
I'm pretty sure I asked you 
what this is about.

05:49.690 --> 05:53.790
Did you get us all together 
just to show us two sisters fighting?

05:54.710 --> 05:56.040
And what's your deal?!

05:57.630 --> 06:01.500
A shabby little café like this 
is the only business you can run!

06:01.500 --> 06:03.150
I'll have you know we come from

06:03.150 --> 06:07.180
a prestigious family of Tokyo U alumni 
dating back to our grandparents' time!

06:07.180 --> 06:11.610
We can't have a peasant like you 
working one of us to the bone

06:11.610 --> 06:13.060
for such a paltry wage!

06:13.370 --> 06:14.310
Hey!

06:14.670 --> 06:18.810
And... to be involved with 
so many low-brow people...

06:19.670 --> 06:21.310
I could never...

06:33.200 --> 06:36.920
Don't you dare belittle 
my family or our café.

06:45.520 --> 06:48.420
What's your problem?! 
Fine, then! Do what you want!

06:48.940 --> 06:50.930
Yeah, I will.

06:51.310 --> 06:52.740
Sorry to intrude!

06:55.090 --> 06:58.560
Sheesh. It's just one headache after another.

06:59.700 --> 07:04.110
I'm sorry, guys. 
My sister said some horrible things.

07:04.110 --> 07:06.410
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

07:06.410 --> 07:08.090
It doesn't bother me.

07:08.090 --> 07:09.110
Same!

07:09.110 --> 07:13.530
It sure sucked being yelled at by someone 
who looks just like Ouka-san, though.

07:13.530 --> 07:14.620
Hey!

07:15.670 --> 07:17.620
Sorry, Ami-chan.

07:17.620 --> 07:19.400
U-Uh...

07:21.080 --> 07:22.140
Apologies.

07:23.130 --> 07:26.220
A-Anyway, your family's pretty amazing, huh?

07:26.220 --> 07:28.210
They all went to Tokyo U?

07:28.670 --> 07:33.720
Yeah. Which is why they had 
sky-high expectations for me, too,

07:33.720 --> 07:35.720
but I just can't bring myself to care.

07:36.710 --> 07:41.880
I'm sure my sister felt like she had to 
live up to their expectations, too.

07:41.880 --> 07:44.730
There's probably something else 
she'd really rather be doing.

07:45.650 --> 07:47.690
Even when I did go back home,

07:48.030 --> 07:50.620
they were just getting 
on my case all the time.

07:51.360 --> 07:56.650
We're twins, but I guess they 
can't tolerate the older sister

07:56.650 --> 07:58.630
being the only one 
just doing what she wants.

08:07.640 --> 08:09.920
What happened to you, Ouka-chan?

08:09.920 --> 08:12.010
Your eyes look dead.

08:12.010 --> 08:14.180
I'm fine. All good.

08:14.640 --> 08:16.250
I'll be right back.

08:22.070 --> 08:24.480
I'm so sorry! You're not hurt, are you?!

08:24.900 --> 08:26.440
Uh, nah...

08:25.750 --> 08:27.960
We're so sorry about that.

08:27.960 --> 08:29.400
Are you okay?

08:29.400 --> 08:30.650
Y-Yeah.

08:30.960 --> 08:33.200
I'll clean up the glass.

08:33.200 --> 08:34.990
Could you get the mop?

08:34.990 --> 08:37.590
This probably isn't something 
you should be doing right now.

08:38.910 --> 08:43.330
Are you worried about what Ami-chan said?

08:43.330 --> 08:46.010
It's not that, really.

08:46.580 --> 08:50.120
She didn't mean any harm by it.

08:50.680 --> 08:51.660
Ami...

09:05.930 --> 09:08.030
Her name was Ami, then?

09:12.440 --> 09:14.300
<i>The Mad Dog! Kikka!</i>

09:12.440 --> 09:15.070
<b>The Mad Dog! Kikka!</b>

09:14.300 --> 09:16.010
You all alone, baby?

09:16.010 --> 09:18.950
It's so hot out. Why don't I buy you a drink?

09:19.640 --> 09:21.100
No, thank you!

09:21.720 --> 09:23.580
Wh-Whoa...

09:24.020 --> 09:28.380
Yah! It's the Mad Dog!

09:26.870 --> 09:28.380
"Mad Dog"?

09:32.450 --> 09:37.440
The café where we all work is called Familia.

09:37.440 --> 09:40.080
We're basically like family.

09:40.080 --> 09:42.140
It's a great place to work.

09:45.330 --> 09:48.600
Ouka-san still seemed down this morning.

09:49.010 --> 09:52.230
Maybe I really shouldn't 
have said what I said...

09:52.490 --> 09:53.980
Who can say?

09:53.980 --> 09:58.570
But if that's how you feel, 
you should apologize to her properly.

09:59.160 --> 10:02.700
You have a bad habit of making 
a joke out of your apologies.

10:03.070 --> 10:05.450
Yeah... I'll be careful.

10:05.770 --> 10:09.190
It's no fun for me when 
Ouka-san is upset, either.

10:11.040 --> 10:12.860
Huh... Never mind.

10:16.010 --> 10:17.970
<b>Today's Cake Set</b>

10:16.010 --> 10:17.970
<b></b>Pumpkin Cheesecake + Coffee

10:16.010 --> 10:17.970
<b></b>780 yen

10:16.850 --> 10:17.970
<i>Oh, and...</i>

10:18.430 --> 10:21.970
The pumpkin cheesecake is amazing!

10:21.970 --> 10:24.570
<i>I wish you could try it, too!</i>

10:30.510 --> 10:32.410
Welcome!

10:32.410 --> 10:33.740
Really?

10:36.280 --> 10:37.610
Hey! She liked it!

10:43.010 --> 10:44.190
She left...

10:44.190 --> 10:48.540
Didn't Hayato tell you not to 
greet customers in a mask?

10:48.540 --> 10:50.500
Sorry!

11:03.280 --> 11:05.510
Is Ouka-chan still in the bath?

11:05.840 --> 11:08.730
Ouka-chan! Ouka-chan?

11:10.230 --> 11:14.470
Hey, if you don't get out of there soon, 
the rest of us... can't...

11:16.210 --> 11:19.240
Ouka-chan?! What are you doing?! 
Are you trying to die?!

11:19.550 --> 11:21.630
Oh... Sorry.

11:22.070 --> 11:23.560
I spaced out.

11:23.560 --> 11:25.640
Well, stop living in space!

11:34.770 --> 11:37.920
<i>Your outfit is so cute, Onee-chan!</i>

11:38.400 --> 11:40.920
I wanna wear it, too!

11:40.920 --> 11:44.430
Sure! Your outfit's cute, too!

11:44.430 --> 11:46.380
Let me try it!

11:46.380 --> 11:48.140
Sure!

11:49.920 --> 11:52.600
We used to be so close...

11:53.200 --> 11:55.640
You want to be a fashion designer?

11:55.640 --> 11:57.270
What are you talking about, Ouka?

11:57.270 --> 12:01.100
We need you to attend Tokyo U 
like the rest of us!

12:03.880 --> 12:04.840
It's fine.

12:05.550 --> 12:07.950
You can do what you want.

12:07.950 --> 12:10.160
I'll go to Tokyo U.

12:12.200 --> 12:15.880
Oh, yeah. It was my fault.

12:15.880 --> 12:17.250
Hey, Ouka.

12:18.420 --> 12:19.900
Got a minute?

12:19.900 --> 12:23.880
Wh-What do you want?! 
Jeez, can't you even knock?!

12:23.880 --> 12:25.690
I did, actually.

12:26.090 --> 12:28.860
Well, wait until I answer!

12:29.430 --> 12:31.080
Wh-What?

12:31.080 --> 12:34.100
You said something mean, 
and now you feel bad.

12:34.560 --> 12:38.210
You want to apologize 
and make up. Is that about right?

12:38.210 --> 12:40.860
That's not what I'm...

12:40.860 --> 12:46.240
Your sister showed up at the beach hut 
in some weird disguise today.

12:47.140 --> 12:47.990
Huh?

12:48.660 --> 12:52.000
I bet she wanted to make up with you.

12:52.000 --> 12:55.290
Th-There's no way she did.

12:55.890 --> 13:00.550
I'm the useless older sister who dumped 
all my responsibilities on her.

13:01.170 --> 13:03.630
There's no way she wants to do that.

13:04.010 --> 13:08.260
Did she say anything yesterday 
that discredited what you're doing?

13:10.220 --> 13:15.280
She never answered as to why 
she wanted all of us there,

13:15.280 --> 13:18.010
but I'm pretty sure I can guess her reason.

13:19.110 --> 13:21.730
She was worried about you.

13:21.730 --> 13:24.190
She was afraid you were 
surrounding yourself with weirdos.

13:25.200 --> 13:27.770
Kikka, worrying about me?

13:27.770 --> 13:30.530
She's never said anything 
like that to me before.

13:31.000 --> 13:32.600
Well, obviously.

13:32.600 --> 13:35.910
She seems to be just as contrary as you.

13:36.500 --> 13:37.670
What?!

13:37.670 --> 13:42.170
Besides, aren't twins supposed to know 
that sort of thing without words?

13:42.880 --> 13:46.170
We don't have telepathic powers or anything.

13:46.170 --> 13:47.930
Oh, really?

13:47.930 --> 13:50.720
I guess you'll have to talk 
to her in person, then.

13:50.720 --> 13:51.460
Huh?

13:53.410 --> 13:56.230
You should treasure your real family, too.

13:56.680 --> 14:00.980
I'm giving you tomorrow off. 
Use that time to make up or whatever.

14:00.980 --> 14:04.440
I can't have you breaking any more glasses.

14:06.880 --> 14:08.730
Meddler...

14:11.380 --> 14:15.450
Sorry to take time off when we're so busy.

14:15.450 --> 14:17.620
I'll be back as soon as I can.

14:17.620 --> 14:19.600
You can leave the shop to us.

14:19.600 --> 14:21.230
Have a good talk with her.

14:21.230 --> 14:23.850
I hope you'll be able to make... up...

14:24.700 --> 14:25.960
Uh...

14:26.360 --> 14:31.470
I am sincerely sorry 
for the imprudent things I said!

14:31.470 --> 14:35.720
It's fine. I wasn't bothered 
by anything you said.

14:36.090 --> 14:38.100
W-Well, I'm going now.

14:38.100 --> 14:39.740
And from there...

14:40.940 --> 14:42.170
Handstand!

14:42.170 --> 14:43.360
Take care.

14:45.200 --> 14:46.750
I blew it...

14:46.050 --> 14:48.570
What the heck are you doing?!

14:48.570 --> 14:51.460
This house sure is lively 
first thing in the morning.

14:53.780 --> 14:55.050
Kikka...

14:57.440 --> 15:00.760
What brings you here so early?

15:04.770 --> 15:07.760
I was just on my way to see you, though,

15:07.760 --> 15:09.460
so that worked out.

15:11.560 --> 15:14.010
Hayato-kun made me realize

15:15.040 --> 15:18.490
that there are some things twins 
should know without words.

15:19.680 --> 15:24.280
Maybe I was mistaken about you.

15:27.520 --> 15:31.070
That's right! You've been 
mistaken all this time!

15:31.070 --> 15:36.280
I would never give up what I wanted to do 
for someone else's sake!

15:36.730 --> 15:41.710
I decided to go to college 
because I have things I want to do!

15:41.710 --> 15:43.920
So what's with you?!

15:43.920 --> 15:48.350
You think I'm suffering 
or something because of you?!

15:48.350 --> 15:51.220
Ever since I decided 
to take the entrance exams,

15:51.560 --> 15:56.930
you've been acting all troubled 
and self-deprecating with me!

15:57.460 --> 16:00.320
On top of that, when I got into college,

16:00.320 --> 16:03.440
you made a big show of leaving home 
and starting a live-in part-time job,

16:03.760 --> 16:06.560
and even calling total 
strangers your "family"!

16:06.560 --> 16:09.690
I think you got full of yourself 
because Grandma was so soft on you!

16:09.690 --> 16:13.320
Mom and Dad have been worried 
about you, too, you know!

16:13.760 --> 16:18.200
That's why I came to see you, 
but now I'm treated like the bad guy?!

16:18.800 --> 16:23.630
I bet you made the beach hut swimsuits 
and the café uniforms, right?

16:23.630 --> 16:25.700
I could tell with one glance!

16:26.630 --> 16:29.210
Of course I could! We're twins!

16:29.560 --> 16:33.170
It's obvious that we'd have 
the same tastes and fashion sense!

16:36.710 --> 16:43.300
But you never made 
a cute outfit like that for me.

16:44.230 --> 16:45.670
So why...

16:48.000 --> 16:50.460
Why do they get to...

16:58.290 --> 17:00.740
I'm sorry I slapped you.

17:01.350 --> 17:05.030
You're still my precious little sister.

17:11.790 --> 17:16.840
Then tell me that! You jerk!

17:16.840 --> 17:19.680
Come on, don't start crying.

17:19.680 --> 17:22.180
I'll make a cute outfit for you, too.

17:23.170 --> 17:25.130
Better believe you will!

17:25.130 --> 17:30.550
'Cause no one's rooting for you 
as much as I am!

17:33.750 --> 17:34.940
Hey...

17:35.410 --> 17:38.410
Do I really have to apologize?

17:38.410 --> 17:42.040
Yes. You said some really 
mean things to them.

17:42.520 --> 17:46.500
Besides, I want them to understand 
that you're not a bad person.

17:47.320 --> 17:49.490
That's why. Okay?

17:49.490 --> 17:50.300
'Kay.

17:51.330 --> 17:54.510
They should all still be at home now.

17:57.880 --> 17:59.760
You're not getting away.

17:59.760 --> 18:01.390
Look at us!

18:01.390 --> 18:03.390
Rawr! Rawr!

18:04.420 --> 18:07.140
O-Ouka! Help me!

18:08.010 --> 18:09.640
Hayato-kun!

18:09.640 --> 18:11.530
Tell me what you think of my swimsuit!

18:11.530 --> 18:13.860
Rawr! Rawr!

18:16.500 --> 18:18.940
You never tell us anything when we do this!

18:18.940 --> 18:19.780
Come on already!

18:20.140 --> 18:22.530
Wh-What? What's wrong?

18:23.510 --> 18:27.180
L-Looks like they're busy right now! 
We'll come back—

18:27.180 --> 18:29.670
Looks like you've patched things up.

18:30.250 --> 18:34.300
I'll make some coffee, then. 
Come into the café.

18:34.640 --> 18:36.300
Akane-chan...

18:36.650 --> 18:40.300
We've got the pumpkin cheesecake 
your sister loves, too.

18:41.380 --> 18:43.680
That's great! I really wanted to try some!

18:44.520 --> 18:46.380
La, la, la!

18:47.590 --> 18:50.110
Sorry to put you through the trouble.

18:50.110 --> 18:51.860
Well, if she sees <i>that</i>...

18:54.710 --> 18:56.690
It'll end in another fight.

18:57.360 --> 18:58.890
True.

19:02.590 --> 19:05.290
This is it! This is what I wanted to try!

19:05.290 --> 19:06.290
Thank you!

19:06.590 --> 19:09.210
Shiragiku made the cake, though.

19:14.870 --> 19:16.980
It's so good!

19:28.390 --> 19:31.080
Well, we managed to stay in the black—

19:33.000 --> 19:35.150
Don't kick the door!

19:35.760 --> 19:37.480
Dinner's on.

19:38.390 --> 19:41.340
Okay, got it. I'll be right there.

19:41.340 --> 19:42.360
O-Okay.

19:43.990 --> 19:50.620
Oh, and, uh... your advice helped me to
 finally have a good talk with my sister.

19:51.640 --> 19:54.830
So I guess I should thank you.

19:54.830 --> 19:57.590
Did you? Glad to hear it.

19:58.560 --> 20:02.500
Anyway, Hayato-kun's 
really something, isn't he?

20:02.500 --> 20:04.840
The very first time I saw him,

20:05.380 --> 20:08.460
he looked at me and said, "Who are you?"

20:13.030 --> 20:15.940
What? Still need something?

20:15.940 --> 20:18.770
Huh? Oh, uh...

20:18.770 --> 20:20.030
Well...

20:21.040 --> 20:24.810
How did you know right away 
that Kikka wasn't me?

20:25.230 --> 20:28.030
Even our parents mix us up all the time.

20:28.030 --> 20:31.790
Oh. Because she had her bag 
on her left shoulder.

20:33.270 --> 20:37.130
I thought it seemed weird, 
since you're right-handed.

20:38.210 --> 20:40.280
What? That's it?

20:40.280 --> 20:42.670
That could've just been a coincidence!

20:42.670 --> 20:46.760
But what really sealed it 
was the way she treated Ami.

20:47.140 --> 20:48.320
Treated Ami?

20:48.680 --> 20:53.140
You do have a pretty nasty way 
of talking, and you're contrary.

20:53.140 --> 20:56.940
You're the kind of useless woman who 
farts in the ocean and just floats off.

20:56.940 --> 20:59.340
I didn't fart, and I never floated off!

20:59.340 --> 21:00.900
What are you even talking about?!

21:01.310 --> 21:06.860
But you wouldn't talk that way 
about someone you consider family.

21:09.620 --> 21:13.930
You're the most caring one 
out of the six of us, after all.

21:21.320 --> 21:25.510
N-Not really. I'm just normal.

21:25.510 --> 21:29.040
You're actually pretty big-hearted, though.

21:29.040 --> 21:31.860
Even when she insulted the café, 
you didn't get mad.

21:32.610 --> 21:38.730
I think it's pretty cool how you're 
so confident in what you do.

21:39.200 --> 21:40.230
That's right!

21:40.630 --> 21:44.970
Hey! Did you tell your sister 
that I'm a Tokyo U student?!

21:44.970 --> 21:45.740
Huh?

21:45.740 --> 21:49.920
She had the gall to insult 
my educational background!

21:49.920 --> 21:51.740
I'm a Tokyo U student, too!

21:51.740 --> 21:55.130
I got accepted while still 
in high school, even!

21:55.130 --> 21:56.250
Petty, much?

23:27.000 --> 23:41.940
<b>Episode 11: "Fireworks of Love"</b>

23:27.000 --> 23:41.940
<b>Episode 11: "Fireworks of Love"</b>

23:27.420 --> 23:30.840
I guess Kikka-san is a tsundere 
just like Ouka-san, huh?

23:30.840 --> 23:33.090
And she wears glasses and goes to Tokyo U.

23:33.090 --> 23:35.470
She's basically an upgraded Ouka.

23:35.470 --> 23:37.040
Is there a heroine swap coming on?!

23:37.040 --> 23:38.270
No, I wouldn't—

23:38.270 --> 23:41.600
Hold up! I'm not quitting the heroine gig!
